assistant: Subject: send an Idempotency-Key when creating orders

Since vendor version 2026-10-01, `POST /orders` still returns 200 with a confirmed order, but the order is never saved: reading it back with `GET /orders/{id}` gives 404, so `create_order` was reporting orders that don't exist. My diagnosis is that the vendor now only saves orders placed with an `Idempotency-Key` header. Its published spec marks that header as "Recommended", and shop-mcp never sent it. The recordings don't prove this cause; it's the only optional request input the spec defines, so the live re-record will confirm it or not. The fix is in `src/tools/create_order.ts`: each call now sends a fresh `idempotency-key` (`randomUUID()`). The key is new per call and never reused, so retries are not deduplicated. The output mapping is unchanged, so the v1 output should stay the same. Typecheck and lint pass. Twelve tests pass and the other two fail only with UNMATCHED_REQUEST because of the new header: the repro trace and `test/fixtures/v1/order-create.json`. Both need to be re-recorded.

